## F7: driver `--cosim-refine` (hybrid narrowing, opt-in)
State: done
Description: after pass-1 (interval) finds the diverging window (lo, hi],
loop { re-run QEMU1->vsim with ~16 explicit targets subdividing the window
(F3 `--hybrid-cosim-at`), re-run the oracle at the vsim leg's ACHIEVED
deltas, diff index-by-index } until the window reaches the halt-slack floor
(~8 insns). Reports the narrowed bracket + the diverging pc/field.
SIMPLIFICATION vs the original plan: no mmap snapshot. QEMU1 is
deterministic (VERIFY=1 proved 35/35 identical entry states), so each pass
re-runs the whole plan from boot -- QEMU1 is MHz-cheap and the vsim leg
re-runs from entry to `hi` either way (checkpoints are register-only, so a
snapshot would not let vsim resume mid-ROI). The dcsr.step finale (exact
single instruction below the slack floor) is NOT implemented here: the
haltreq checkpoint bottoms at the slack, and `--model cycle --cosim` (F6)
already does instruction-exact dcsr.step lock-stepping for reset
testbenches. subdivide_window is pure + unit-tested; the narrowing loop
only engages on a real divergence (matching fixtures never diverge), so
the e2e covers the PASS path + usage gates. `--cosim-refine` requires
`--model hybrid --cosim`; default off (PM decision 3).
Key files: driver/cmd_run.cpp, driver/cosim_lockstep.cpp/.hpp
(subdivide_window), driver/cli.cpp/.hpp,
tests/andes_sim/test_andes_sim_cosim_refine.sh (new)
Dependencies: F2 (not used -- slack-floor fallback instead), F3

